#import "pele/lib.notc" as pele;
#import "typst/lib.notc" as typst;

= Documentation components

The book keeps the Pele diagram and Typst math components under
`do`. They are copies of the Notist modules used by Icy Bot, so
the book can render Mermaid-style diagrams and Typst formulas without vendoring
a second toolchain.

Both components load their pinned browser libraries from a CDN the first time a
page renders. Building the book does not need network access; viewing the
generated diagrams and formulas does.

## Pele diagrams

`pele.diagram` accepts Mermaid source and supports the `auto`, `light` and
`dark` themes:

#pele.diagram(r#"""
flowchart LR
    source[Game files] --> decode[Decode]
    decode --> data[Render-facing data]
    data --> app[Application]
"""#)

## Typst math

The project manifest replaces `notist.math` with `typst.math`, so inline and
block math use Typst syntax throughout the book. Inline formula:
$x^2 + y^2 = z^2$.

A block formula can select the result type explicitly:

#typst.math<BlockContent>("sum_(i=1)^n i = frac(n(n+1), 2)")

The full Typst entry point is also available for arbitrary markup:

#typst.svg(r#"""
= Typst SVG

The `typst.svg` function renders complete Typst markup, not only formulas.
"""#)
